{"type":"root","children":[{"type":"heading","depth":1,"id":"debugging-styles","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Debugging styles"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"A style is not doing what you expect. In rough order of likelihood:"}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"1-is-the-module-compiled","children":[{"type":"text","value":"1 · Is the module compiled?"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"If "},{"type":"inlineComponent","name":"inline-code","tagName":"md-inline-code","attributes":{},"children":[],"properties":{"html":"<span class=\"th-token th-function\">css</span>()","source":"css()"}},{"type":"text","value":" runs in a module the compiler never saw, it throws with a message that\nsays exactly that. If you see the error, the fix is the adapter: "},{"type":"inlineComponent","name":"inline-code","tagName":"md-inline-code","attributes":{},"children":[],"properties":{"html":"<span class=\"th-token th-function\">kirana</span>()","source":"kirana()"}},{"type":"text","value":" must\nbe in the bundler's plugin list, and before the framework plugin."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"2-is-the-element-yours","children":[{"type":"text","value":"2 · Is the element yours?"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineComponent","name":"inline-code","tagName":"md-inline-code","attributes":{},"children":[],"properties":{"html":"sx","source":"sx"}},{"type":"text","value":" on a component from a package does nothing. The compiler warns\n("},{"type":"inlineComponent","name":"inline-code","tagName":"md-inline-code","attributes":{},"children":[],"properties":{"html":"sx-on-external-component","source":"sx-on-external-component"}},{"type":"text","value":"), so check the terminal, and see\n"},{"type":"link","href":"/docs/styling/external-components","children":[{"type":"text","value":"styling other people's components"}]},{"type":"text","value":"."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"3-did-a-merge-keep-an-entry-you-meant-to-replace","children":[{"type":"text","value":"3 · Did a merge keep an entry you meant to replace?"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The most common surprise: a later "},{"type":"inlineComponent","name":"inline-code","tagName":"md-inline-code","attributes":{},"children":[],"properties":{"html":"<span class=\"th-token th-property\">color</span>: <span class=\"th-token th-string\">&quot;grey&quot;</span>","source":"color: \"grey\""}},{"type":"text","value":" replaces only the base entry, so\nan earlier "},{"type":"inlineComponent","name":"inline-code","tagName":"md-inline-code","attributes":{},"children":[],"properties":{"html":":hover","source":":hover"}},{"type":"text","value":" colour still applies. Write "},{"type":"inlineComponent","name":"inline-code","tagName":"md-inline-code","attributes":{},"children":[],"properties":{"html":"{ <span class=\"th-token th-string\">&quot;*&quot;</span>: <span class=\"th-token th-literal\">null</span>, <span class=\"th-token th-property\">base</span>: <span class=\"th-token th-string\">&quot;grey&quot;</span> }","source":"{ \"*\": null, base: \"grey\" }"}},{"type":"text","value":" when\nyou mean \"and nothing else\"; "},{"type":"link","href":"/docs/styling/merging","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Merging"}]},{"type":"text","value":" has the rule."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"4-ask-the-compiler","children":[{"type":"text","value":"4 · Ask the compiler"}]},{"type":"component","name":"code","tagName":"md-code","attributes":{},"children":[],"properties":{"source":"kirana trace src/components/card.tsx:24 padding-top","lang":"bash","html":"<span class=\"th-token th-prompt\">$</span> <span class=\"th-token th-command\">kirana</span> trace src/components/card.tsx:24 padding-top","variant":"terminal"}},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"It lists every candidate declaration for that property, marks the winner, and\nnames the ladder step that decided. If your value is not in the list at all, the\nproblem is upstream: the style is not on that element."}]},{"type":"component","name":"figure-trace","attributes":{},"children":[]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"5-check-the-conditions","children":[{"type":"text","value":"5 · Check the conditions"}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"A condition as a "},{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"top-level key"}]},{"type":"text","value":" is an error, and the message says so."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"A state beats a breakpoint: that is the ladder, not a bug."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"A relation read needs its anchor on the element whose state you are reading."}]}]}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"6-look-at-the-css","children":[{"type":"text","value":"6 · Look at the CSS"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The stylesheet is plain CSS with one declaration per rule, so devtools tell you\nthe truth quickly: inspect the element, read the class list, and look for the\ndeclaration. A class that is present but crossed out is a precedence question\n(step 4, ask "},{"type":"inlineComponent","name":"inline-code","tagName":"md-inline-code","attributes":{},"children":[],"properties":{"html":"trace","source":"trace"}},{"type":"text","value":"). A declaration that is missing entirely is a compile\nquestion (check the terminal)."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"7-animations-that-do-nothing","children":[{"type":"text","value":"7 · Animations that do nothing"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Transition the property you actually set: "},{"type":"inlineComponent","name":"inline-code","tagName":"md-inline-code","attributes":{},"children":[],"properties":{"html":"translate","source":"translate"}},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineComponent","name":"inline-code","tagName":"md-inline-code","attributes":{},"children":[],"properties":{"html":"scale","source":"scale"}},{"type":"text","value":" and "},{"type":"inlineComponent","name":"inline-code","tagName":"md-inline-code","attributes":{},"children":[],"properties":{"html":"rotate","source":"rotate"}},{"type":"text","value":" are\nnot "},{"type":"inlineComponent","name":"inline-code","tagName":"md-inline-code","attributes":{},"children":[],"properties":{"html":"transform","source":"transform"}},{"type":"text","value":". See "},{"type":"link","href":"/docs/styling/animation","children":[{"type":"text","value":"animation"}]},{"type":"text","value":"."}]}],"headings":[{"id":"debugging-styles","text":"Debugging styles","level":1},{"id":"1-is-the-module-compiled","text":"1 · Is the module compiled?","level":2},{"id":"2-is-the-element-yours","text":"2 · Is the element yours?","level":2},{"id":"3-did-a-merge-keep-an-entry-you-meant-to-replace","text":"3 · Did a merge keep an entry you meant to replace?","level":2},{"id":"4-ask-the-compiler","text":"4 · Ask the compiler","level":2},{"id":"5-check-the-conditions","text":"5 · Check the conditions","level":2},{"id":"6-look-at-the-css","text":"6 · Look at the CSS","level":2},{"id":"7-animations-that-do-nothing","text":"7 · Animations that do nothing","level":2}]}
